  "notes": "The issue added a check-in stop, so a day can show the party checking in at the hotel before a later event. It started at 740 words and reached 1,625 by the time PR #183 opened, over 7 versions in about four hours on 2026-10-27. Nothing was added after. Half the words are settled questions (I169-12 to I169-16), each a struck proposal followed by Joe's answer. Those answers are clearly the task, not history. Do I169-17 says to write them into the design docs, and they hold the design, such as the new checkIn kind and how the stop-order check splits a day. A separate Decided section (I169-6, I169-7) holds two choices made outside questions. A \"What happened\" section records the live session that showed the bug (I169-3), and Done when points back to it (I169-20). The PR description copies Do and Done when (P183-d1 to d8) and adds detailed results (P183-d9 to d15). The decisions comment holds 11 decisions, and 4 name the doc they went into (P183-c0, c1, c2, c11). The rest are code-level choices. It also has wording pointers for Joe and one item set aside into #177 (P183-c14). Results went into the PR description only."
